WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.250
Lights down.

2
00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:04.950
The cinema screen fills
with a huge, bright picture.

3
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:07.470
Follow the beam back into the projector.

4
00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:10.430
Inside, the light hits a small chip.

5
00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:12.630
Zoom in, and closer still.

6
00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:15.830
The chip is covered in
tiny square mirrors.

7
00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:18.550
Up to 8.8 million of them.

8
00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:22.190
So how can a grid of mirrors
make a moving picture?

9
00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:23.670
Do the mirrors glow?

10
00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:28.130
In this mission, you'll see how output
devices present results in a form people

11
00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:30.530
can see, hear or use.

12
00:00:30.580 --> 00:00:33.390
You'll meet screens,
printers and speakers,

13
00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:34.990
and how each works.

14
00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:39.610
And back in that projector, you'll find
each tiny mirror matches one pixel of

15
00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:40.650
the picture.

16
00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:45.520
Your mission: explain how millions of
tiny mirrors can make a cinema picture.
